  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coordinated Action on Disability in Liberia (CAD-L)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Coordinated Action on Disability in Liberia (CAD-L)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">AIFO &#xe4;r en internationell ickestatlig organisation baserad i Bologna, Italien med landskontor i Monrovia, Liberia. Projektet &#x201d;Coordinated Action on Disability in Liberia&#x201d; (CAD-L) har en l&#xf6;ptid fr&#xe5;n 1 september 2021 till 31 augusti 2025 med en total finansieringsram p&#xe5; 34 700 000 SEK. Sverige &#xe4;r ensam givare till projektet. Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let f&#xf6;r projektet &#xe4;r att &apos;persons with disabilities act as advocates and agents of change for an equitable and inclusive Liberia&apos;. Projektets specifika &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att &apos;Personer med funktionsvariation &#xe4;r till en st&#xf6;rre utstr&#xe4;ckning ekonomiskt oberoende&apos;. F&#xf6;r att n&#xe5; det specifika m&#xe5;let har tre delresultat identifierats;

1. Allm&#xe4;nheten har &#xe4;ndrad attityd till det socioekonomiska bidraget funktionsvarierade ger till Liberia

2. Sociala akt&#xf6;rer har ett definierat kollektivavtal om anst&#xe4;ndigt arbete f&#xf6;r funktionsvarierande

3. Konkreta &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder som har vidtagits av ansvarsb&#xe4;rare och civilsamh&#xe4;llsorganisationer har skapat nya m&#xf6;jligheter f&#xf6;r personer med funktionsvariation g&#xe4;llande syssels&#xe4;ttning, egenf&#xf6;retagande och entrepren&#xf6;rskap inom den offentliga och privata sektorn.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution &apos;Coordinated Action on Disability in Liberia&apos; (CAD-L) is a project by AIFO an International NGO based in Bologna Italy with country office in Monrovia, Liberia. The project has a duration 1 September 2021 to 31 August 2025 with a total funding envelop of 34 700 000 SEK of which Sweden is the sole donor. The overall goal of the project is &apos;persons with disabilities act as advocates and agents of change for an equitable and inclusive Liberia&apos;.   The project will directly fulfil the specific objective &apos;Persons with disabilities have improved economic independence&apos;. In order to achieve its specific objectives, the project will achieve three intermediary outcomes: 1. The general public has changed attitudes towards the socio-economic contribution PWDs make to Liberia; 2. Social actors in Liberia are able to negotiate and conclude a collective agreement on decent work for PWDs  and 3. Concrete steps taken by Duty Bearers and CSOs have created new opportunities for persons with disabilities employment, self-employment and entrepreneurship in the public and private sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project overall objective:

Persons with disabilities act as advocates and agents of change for an equitable and inclusive Liberia

Project specific objective:

PWDs have improved economic independence

INTERMEDIATE OUTCOME 1. The general public has changed attitudes towards the socio-economic contribution PWDs make to Liberia

INTERMEDIATE OUTCOME 2. Social actors have a defined collective agreement on decent work for PWDs

INTERMEDIATE OUTCOME 3. Concrete steps taken by Duty Bearers (DBs) and CSOs have created new opportunities for PWDs employment, self-employment and entrepreneurship in the public and private sectors</narrative>
  </description>
